Package: shinyOAuthDB
Title: Use Database OAuth Access in Shiny Apps
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R: person("Luka", "Koning", email = "koningluka@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"))
Description: Query databases and data platforms in Shiny using each visitor's
    own OAuth authorization. Provides 'DBI' connections for SQL queries and
    supplies user credentials to 'fabricQueryR' and 'brickster' functions.
    Connects to CockroachDB through 'RPostgres' using visitor JWT access tokens.
    Queries SAP HANA and HANA Cloud through SAP HANA ODBC with each visitor's
    JWT access token.
    Queries SingleStore and SingleStore Helios through SingleStore ODBC
    using each visitor's JWT access token.
    Uses 'shinyOAuth' for sign-in and token renewal, and manages connections
    within each Shiny session. Supports Oracle Database OAuth access through
    Oracle ODBC and protected Oracle REST Data Services resources over HTTPS.
    Supports Azure SQL, Azure Database for MySQL, Microsoft Fabric,
    BigQuery, Redshift, Databricks, Snowflake, Trino, and PostgreSQL, including self-hosted
    PostgreSQL with native OAuth and Azure PostgreSQL. Reads PostgreSQL tables
    and calls exposed database functions through PostgREST and Supabase's
    Data API with visitor access tokens and project publishable keys. Supports StarRocks
    JWT authentication through MySQL Connector/ODBC, and ClickHouse queries
    through JWT-enabled HTTPS endpoints. Connects to remote DuckDB servers
    through the Quack protocol with OAuth access tokens. Queries remote
    libSQL and compatible Turso endpoints using each visitor's access token.
    Queries CrateDB's HTTPS SQL interface with per-user JWT access tokens.
    Searches Elasticsearch using visitor JWT access tokens, with SQL and
    ES|QL queries and optional JWT realm client authentication.
    Searches OpenSearch
    indexes and runs its SQL plugin queries using each visitor's bearer token.
    Queries Salesforce CRM with SOQL and Data Cloud with SQL through the
    Query Connect API using each visitor's Salesforce authorization.
